# IDEs & Editors
# .vscode/ is deliberately tracked: launch.json is how a contributor runs the
# extension host, so it belongs in the repo rather than in each clone.
# The fixtures workspace is the exception: it's the `workspaceFolder` the
# integration suite runs against, and any test that updates configuration at
# ConfigurationTarget.Workspace (see tests/integration/watcher.test.ts)
# leaves VS Code's own settings.json behind there — a test artifact, not
# something to commit.
tests/fixtures/.vscode/
.idea/
.zed/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

